  "final_text": "The space, rule, and enable step are all done, and I read the rule back to confirm.\n\n- **Space:** `e2e-haiku-9b7a4273` was created with the same name as its id. I didn't set a solution or description.\n- **Rule:** \"E2E 8f1c903a flight watch\" (id `82d5e36e-04f4-4d4e-9ce9-68b3be51a085`) is an `.es-query` rule with consumer `stackAlerts` in that space.\n- **Condition:** it counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_flights` using `timestamp` as the time field, over a 5-minute window, and fires when the count is greater than 0.\n- **State:** `enabled: true`.\n\nChoices I made that you didn't specify:\n- The query is `match_all`, so the rule counts every document in the window.\n- The schedule is every 1 minute, which is the tool default.\n- Sample data may need to be loaded in the space for the index to contain documents.",
